maya: Heads-up — I'm opening a tiny docs PR that consolidates our 429 + timeout troubleshooting snippets into one compact 'fallback recipes' section. Need a quick review on the SDK examples and one link correction.
tomas: ack. pinging @maya — which file path?
maya: /docs/errors/troubleshooting.md (I moved two snippets into a new 'fallbacks' heading). The main items: (1) JS retry + backoff snippet for 429s (2) Python context trimming example for large prompts (3) a short note about switching to a 'compatible_model' fallback when capacity is low.
priya: can you paste the JS snippet here so I can sanity-check?
maya: sure — here's the current snippet I added:
```javascript
// 429-safe generation with exponential backoff + fallback
async function generateWithFallback(client, opts) {
  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 4; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await client.generate(opts);
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status === 429) {
        await sleep(100 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
        if (attempt === 2) {
          // try lighter model
          opts.model = "gpt-light-compat";
        }
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
  throw new Error("max attempts");
}
```
priya: quick review: look ok conceptually. small nits: we prefer client.responses.generate in newer SDKs and err.status_code is what our SDK sets. Also maybe call out a jitter to avoid thundering herd.
tomas: +1 — also suggest switching to 429-specific Retry-After header handling if present.
maya: good points — I can update the snippet. here's the tiny python helper I added for context trimming: 
```python
# trim context to last N tokens before call
def trim_prompt(prompt, max_tokens=3000):
    return prompt[-max_tokens:]
```
priya: probably worth a one-liner explaining why we choose last N tokens vs first N tokens (preserve the most recent user intent).
dan: FYI I checked the link that broke: docs page was still linking to /old-runbook. There's no redirect in mkdocs. I can add a redirect rule or update the link — which do you prefer?
maya: prefer updating the link target in the markdown to /errors/fallbacks and adding a tiny note in the changelog. If infra prefers redirects we can add them later.
docs-bot: lint: docs/errors/troubleshooting.md: line 128: broken link to /old-runbook -> 404
priya: one more suggestion — add an observability callout: capture model.variant and fallback reason (429 vs timeout vs ctx-trim) in whatever logging/metric you surface so we can detect fallback regressions.
maya: added a 2-line paragraph about that and a sample metric name: `fallback.count{reason=429,variant=gpt-light-compat}`. Also added a short decision blurb under 'when to trim context' about reducing system prompts vs user history.
tomas: approve from SDK-snippet POV after the minor edits (status_code + responses.generate + jitter + Retry-After). :shipit: 
maya: thanks — I'll push the fixes and update the PR description. merging once docs-bot passes. Will ping the infra team to add the redirect if they want one. :thumbsup:
